          ],
          "x": "A restored 1950s lever machine."
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "t": "h2",
        "r": [
         280,
         509,
         720,
         28
        ],
        "x": "The modern shot"
       },
       {
        "t": "p",
        "r": [
         280,
         557,
         720,
         102
        ],
        "x": "Faema's E61 group head introduced pump-driven brewing and thermal stability in 1961, a design so durable that new machines still ship with it today. Specialty caf\u00e9s now argue about pressure profiling and flow control, but the fundamentals have not moved: roughly nine bars, ninety-three degrees, and thirty seconds."
       },
       {
        "t": "p",
        "r": [
         280,
         676,
         720,
         51
        ],
        "x": "What has changed is measurement. Refractometers, scales, and pressure transducers turned folklore into repeatable recipes, and home machines inherited the instrumentation."
       }
